  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I haven't run it in a browser, so the rendering is unchecked. The sphere uses a custom GLSL material (`material.custom`) with additive blending and no depth write. It has a cyan fresnel rim, scanlines that scroll upward through a `clk` uniform updated every frame, and a low base alpha for translucency. A metallic PBR cube sits inside and rotates. The background is dark. The floor is a low-roughness metallic plane lit by a cyan point light under the sphere, plus bloom, so it should pick up the glow. The camera is a perspective camera framing the sphere. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` resolves and one more animation frame has passed. `createAuraApp` runs the render loop itself, so I did not add my own `requestAnimationFrame` loop.",
